# Playtest: Cube Jump v1.0-playtest

Build: `cube-jump.zip` from release `v1.0-playtest` of world/producer, sha256 `95ae15c038e69187334fe0dcaa76546265572c07293ed4f8b8de75301a230e41`.
Unzipped: one file, `index.html` (7354 bytes) at the zip root.
Played: headless Chromium 156 (Playwright 1.64) opened from `file:///.../index.html`, no server, 1000x500 viewport. Real keyboard events (`keyboard.press('Space')`) were used, in real time.
Evidence: `reports/evidence/*.png`, and the scripts `play.py` (live run), `fair.py` (jump windows) and `mc.py` (noisy-player simulation).
Not done: no human with a physical keyboard, no Firefox, no audio check. Headless Chromium can't confirm how the jump feels in hand.

